fake_quick_sync_setup.py
# Local health/diagnostics record (dev runs write it to the repo root;
# frozen builds write it to the per-user config dir). Never committed.
diagnostics/

# Audit runs: track the RESULT, never the course material.
#
# The findings, the reports and the per-row logs ARE the audit - they are what
# a later session re-reads to adjudicate a finding, and losing them means the
# work has to be redone on a rented machine. They are also small (~4 MB of
# results, ~38 MB with logs across every run to date).
#
# What is excluded and why:
#   downloads/        the student's actual Canvas course material - GBs of it,
#                     and not ours to redistribute
#   browser-profile/  Chrome profile: cookies and session state for a real
#                     logged-in Canvas account. NEVER commit this.
#   config/           the run's app config dir. No token today (checked), but
#                     it is exactly where one lands if the keyring path fails,
#                     so it stays out on principle rather than on inspection.
#   disk_*.json       per-file inventories with md5s - 499 MB and regenerable
#   evidence/rows/    harvested per-row folder copies - 33 MB, same reason
#   screenshots/      130 MB of PNGs
#   _snapshots/ _screens/   golden folders and UI renders, GBs, regenerable
#
# NOTE the trade: `matrix recheck` re-derives findings from disk_*.json, so a
# historical run cannot be re-checked once its evidence is gone. The findings
# and logs it already produced remain, which is what adjudication actually
# needs.
#
# NOTE the `/*` forms below are deliberate. Git will not descend into an
# EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so a negation inside one can never re-include
# anything - the same trap `.claude/*` documents. Excluding the CONTENTS
# instead leaves the directory itself readable, so the two keepers below
# work: the debug log, and the health log + session state.
_audit_runs/**/downloads/*
!_audit_runs/**/downloads/debug_log.txt
_audit_runs/**/browser-profile/
_audit_runs/**/config/*
!_audit_runs/**/config/diagnostics/
_audit_runs/**/evidence/rows/
_audit_runs/**/evidence/screenshots/
_audit_runs/**/disk_*.json
_audit_runs/**/samples/
_audit_runs/_snapshots/
_audit_runs/_screens/
# UI review renders (scripts/capture_completion_gallery.py). Regenerated on
# demand and ~18 MB of PNGs - deliberately NOT under docs/, which is the
# published website.
ui-review/

# Virtualenvs. NOT ignored until 2026-08-10, and it mattered: the macOS audit
# machine builds .venv INSIDE the repo, so `git add -A` (which the audit agent
# is instructed to run) saw ~10,000 files and would have committed the whole
# interpreter, native wheels and all. Ignored here rather than in a local
# exclude so every machine that clones this is protected.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# VS Code Remote-SSH server payload, if it ever lands inside the tree.
.vscode-server/

# The macOS Office Automation permission record (runtime state, machine-specific)
macos_permission_setup.json
